/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  Modified UNIFAC (Dortmund) subgroups: R_k, Q_k and main group -- 85 subgroups.

  SOURCE (the ONLY one): Gmehling, J.; Li, J.; Schiller, M. "A Modified UNIFAC
  Model. 2. Present Parameter Matrix and Results for Different Thermodynamic
  Properties", Ind. Eng. Chem. Res. 32 (1993) 178-193, doi:10.1021/ie00013a024,
  Table III, pp. 182-183 ("R_k- and Q_k-Parameters and Group Assignment for the
  Modified UNIFAC (Dortmund) Method").  Read at the page (page image, not the
  scan's text layer).  Each value is transcribed as printed.

  LICENCE.  Only the parameters printed in that paper (and Weidlich & Gmehling,
  Ind. Eng. Chem. Res. 26 (1987) 1372) are entered.  The later Dortmund
  revisions (the 2002-2022 matrices) are distributed under licence and are NOT
  entered from any source; a group pair this paper does not print is REFUSED by
  name at run time, never filled from another table (DEV.md 4c C408 (c)).

  NAMES.  Subgroup names are the paper's, made tokenizer-safe: OH (p/s/t) ->
  OH_p, OH_s, OH_t; the ether CH-O (printed "CHO", the same as the aldehyde
  CHO) -> CH-O; CHtripleC and CtripleC are the triple-bond groups (the paper's
  main group 34); parens -> '_'; the half-weight ring-ether groups 83 and 84
  ([CH2]1/2) are written with `h` for the "1/2".  `number` is the paper's own
  subgroup number, `mainGroup` its main-group number (the paper's Table IV
  index).  The decomposition of a component is its own record's `groups {
  unifacDortmund (...) }` block, never this file's.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

provenance
{
    origin  literature;
    source  "Gmehling, Li & Schiller, Ind. Eng. Chem. Res. 32 (1993) 178, Table III, pp. 182-183";
    reuse   "values transcribed from the printed table; the later licensed Dortmund revisions are not entered";
}

mainGroups
(
